Drop the leftover debug printf in the curses keyboard driver.

curses_uninit() announces "uninitializing" on stdout every time an aalib
program using the curses driver exits. It lands after endwin() has already
restored the screen, so it is plain garbage on the user's terminal — bb
prints it over the shell prompt every time it quits.

--- a/src/aacurkbd.c
+++ b/src/aacurkbd.c
@@ -59,7 +59,6 @@
 }
 static void curses_uninit(aa_context * c)
 {
-    printf("uninitializing\n");
     keypad(stdscr, FALSE);
     nodelay(stdscr, FALSE);
 #ifdef SIGWINCH
